  "published": "2026-11-19T05:45:59.517Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "First release: WebAuthnTestAuthenticator, a software authenticator for a test project's passkey and security-key endpoint tests. It reads the creation or request options an endpoint returned, typed or as JSON, and answers with the body the browser's PublicKeyCredential.toJSON() posts, signed ES256 or RS256 with attestation none. Its sign count, user verification, backup flags, user handle and transports are settable, so a test can make the verifier refuse it, and it refuses the options its README's Refusals table lists, as a real authenticator or browser does. Requires EasyReasy.Auth 5.15.0. See https://github.com/AdamTovatt/easy-reasy/blob/auth-testing-v1.0.0/EasyReasy.Auth.Testing/README.md",
